      "claim": "Polygraph (lie‑detector) machines record physiological signals such as heart rate, blood pressure, respiration and skin conductance, but they do not measure deception directly.",
      "evidence": "Technical specifications of polygraph devices (American Polygraph Association) and reviews by the American Psychological Association show they monitor autonomic activity, an indirect proxy for stress, not the cognitive act of lying.",
